config BR2_PACKAGE_THINGINO_ISP_GUARD
	bool "Boot guard for the open ISP stack"
	default n
	depends on BR2_PACKAGE_THINGINO_ISP_OPEN
	help
	  Install /etc/init.d/S10isp-guard, a crash-loop guard for the
	  open-tx-isp kernel modules: a boot that crashes or resets before
	  it has run 300 s with the ISP opened by a streamer (timps, prudynt,
	  raptor, ...) makes the next boot skip the ISP and sensor modules
	  and timps (the camera stays reachable over SSH and the web UI;
	  "S10isp-guard clear" re-arms it). Planned reboots and firmware
	  upgrades do not count; the first boot of a new image starts with a
	  clean guard state. The u-boot variable isp_open=auto|manual|off
	  selects the behaviour.

	  Meant for development and bring-up of the open stack. Do not
	  enable it on cameras that must keep streaming through repeated
	  power loss: two reboots within five minutes leave the streamer
	  off until someone clears the guard.
